Queued interstitial milestone after M6
--------------------------------------
## Vector Authoring, Multi-Selection & Grouping UX

Promote this before View Models / Data Binding because it closes current everyday drawing/editing gaps in the editor.

### Stage coordinates / position readout
- Show pointer world coordinates for the active artboard in the stage/status bar (X / Y).
- Show selected object's authored transform position clearly in the Inspector.
- For multi-selection, expose deterministic selection bounds/center without inventing authored values.
- Coordinate readout must use the same world/client transform as renderer and hit testing.

### Rive-style Pen / Draw Path lifecycle
- A valid draft path must not disappear merely because the user changes tools.
- Match Rive's Pen lifecycle: pressing Esc after >=2 vertices finishes/commits the path; an incomplete one-point draft may cancel.
- Switching tools with a valid draft should deterministically commit/finalize rather than silently discard it.
- Click places a straight vertex; click+drag creates Bezier handles immediately.
- Closing a path by targeting the first vertex must be supported.
- Persistent path creation must go through the canonical command/Store path and be one undoable authored operation.

### Edit Vertices mode
- Enter with a selected path enters Edit Vertices mode; provide a visible Done Editing action.
- Vertices remain stable-addressable entities.
- Drag vertex to reposition.
- Drag Bezier handles to reshape curves.
- Support explicit handle modes compatible with Rive concepts: straight, mirrored, detached, asymmetric.
- Ctrl/Cmd+click vertex toggles straight/mirrored where valid.
- Ctrl/Cmd+click handle removes that handle.
- Alt/Option+click handle detaches it.
- Pen Alt/Option+click vertex deletes the vertex.
- Add/remove-vertex operations must exist in the canonical command registry (not UI-only mutations).
- Expose straight-vertex corner radius and allow direct dragging/Inspector editing; define deterministic conversion to explicit curve vertices when needed.
- Open/close path and reverse-direction operations should be machine-readable and undoable.

### Multi-selection
- Store/editor selection must support multiple stable typed refs rather than one selectedId only.
- Shift+click add/remove selection.
- Empty-stage marquee selection.
- Deep selection must remain possible for nested groups.
- Focus/visibility/lock behavior must stay stable under multi-selection.

### Group / ungroup
- Windows/Linux Ctrl+G and macOS Cmd+G group the current selection.
- Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+G ungroups.
- Grouping preserves every child's rendered world transform and draw order.
- Ungrouping preserves rendered world transforms and deterministic hierarchy order.
- Group/ungroup are canonical commands, one undoable operation, AI-readable, stable-ref based and name-independent.

### Overlay / low-zoom ergonomics
- Distinguish authored artwork from editor-only overlays.
- Authored fills/strokes scale normally with camera zoom unless an explicit future non-scaling-stroke feature says otherwise.
- Selection handles, vertices, Bezier handles, bones and controls may use bounded screen-space sizing for usability, but must not alter authored geometry.
- Add a clear way to hide rig/editor overlays (and/or a final-playback view) so low-zoom artwork can be inspected without controls visually dominating it.

Mandatory tests should cover save/load, undo/redo, 10%–800% zoom, nested transforms, multi-selection/group transform preservation, pen Esc/tool-switch finalization, Bezier handle editing, and UI/AI command parity.

